  "scope": "T and R are native power fractions for the matched axial drive. Changes subtract the 32-segment response from the 48-segment response and use the 32-segment power as the relative baseline. The changed segmentation remeshes the central region. The earlier thickness contrast provides scale only. The 200 nm device has no 48-segment result, so its paired contrast is unresolved.",
  "limits": "Finite saved calculations at one frequency with the original physical sections and end planes. Normalized coordinates are used only for displacement matching; T and R are fractions of native incident power. This single-drive comparison leaves all-channel and complex-response failures in force. Weak reflection and relative changes near zero remain sensitive to discretization. Spatial and frequency convergence, a reflection floor, and continuous branch identity remain unresolved."
